  "summary": [
    "C10: five dependency-coupled graph-class closure sources, not five equivalent predicates. Two isomorphism-closure adapters and two strong hereditary adapters share the corresponding explicit canonical interfaces. Packing X155 retains induced closure ONLY. Classes are arbitrary sgraph-to-Prop predicates, with no nonempty/properness/decidability guard.",
    "Reuse upstream diso (a Type-valued bijection preserving both edge directions) and induced. X3 packs diso in inhabited and orders its premises differently; its iff is constructive. Minor uses the explicit witness directly. Strong hereditary_class is iso_closed AND induced_closed. No converse from induced-only closure is asserted without iso closure.",
    "All five source bodies and all three whole rows are frozen. Preserve X3 solved/done, X220 disproved/done, and X155 open/BLOCKED states, every complete row body/doc block, the X155 empty-class defect and the refuted-direction e078 annotation. No statement repair or new formal resolution is performed.",
    "The complete X3 Original composes frozen C10 hereditary closure with existing C9 frozen chi_bounded, retaining the same existential class and polynomial negation. The prior C9 snapshot stays verbatim with reciprocal history notes. x3_iso is unchanged, so A6 complement snapshots and the C9 complementation Original remain outside this closure.",
    "Public-only examples cover empty/all/order-bounded classes, isomorphism transport, union/intersection, and an iso-closed exact-two-vertex class rejected by induced closure. Exact witness/domain types, all four whole iff types, frozen/live closures and both frozen/live X155 empty-class refutations require pinned-kernel checks and independent step-10/coordinator review."
  ],
